<div class="Section1">
<h1>Phase 3: Project Design Phase</h1>
<p style="font-size: 13pt; color: #4a5568;"><strong>ContentGen (BlogNest) System Architecture &amp; Schemas</strong></p>

<h2>1. Layered Architecture Model (Epic 1)</h2>
<ol>
  <li><strong>Interface:</strong> Postman, Thunder Client, and web clients.</li>
  <li><strong>Express Server Gateway:</strong> Port 5000 monitor, CORS, body parsers, rate limiters.</li>
  <li><strong>Authentication &amp; Role Matrix Middleware:</strong> JWT verification, RBAC guards, and express-validator.</li>
  <li><strong>Granular Services Layer:</strong> Blog lifecycle manager, comment queue, media registry, system reports.</li>
  <li><strong>Database Interface Layer:</strong> Mongoose ODM with compound text indexing and schema assertions.</li>
  <li><strong>AI Flow Layer:</strong> GeminiService client connecting to Google Gemini AI.</li>
  <li><strong>BlogGenerator with AI:</strong> Automated blog content generation pipeline.</li>
</ol>

<h2>2. Entity-Relationship (ER) Schema Specifications</h2>
<h3>1. User Entity</h3>
<ul>
  <li><code>_id</code>: Primary Key (ObjectId)</li>
  <li><code>name</code>: String, Required</li>
  <li><code>email</code>: String, Required, Unique</li>
  <li><code>password</code>: String, Hashed with bcrypt, Required</li>
  <li><code>role</code>: String enum (admin, editor, author, reader), Default: "reader"</li>
  <li><code>timestamps</code>: true</li>
</ul>

<h3>2. Post Entity</h3>
<ul>
  <li><code>_id</code>: Primary Key (ObjectId)</li>
  <li><code>userID</code>: Foreign Key referencing User Collection</li>
  <li><code>name</code>: String, Required (represents Title)</li>
  <li><code>photo</code>: Object/String pathway link</li>
  <li><code>message</code>: String, Core content body</li>
  <li><code>likes</code>: Number, Default: 0</li>
  <li><code>status</code>: String enum (draft, pending, scheduled, published)</li>
  <li><code>timestamps</code>: true</li>
</ul>

<h3>3. Comment Entity</h3>
<ul>
  <li><code>_id</code>: Primary Key (ObjectId)</li>
  <li><code>postID</code>: Foreign Key referencing Post Collection</li>
  <li><code>userID</code>: Foreign Key referencing User Collection</li>
  <li><code>content</code>: String, Required</li>
  <li><code>status</code>: String enum (approved, pending, spam), Default: "approved"</li>
  <li><code>timestamps</code>: true</li>
</ul>

<h2>3. Key Structural Mappings</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>User to Post (One-to-Many):</strong> An author can submit multiple blog documents.</li>
  <li><strong>User to Comment (One-to-Many):</strong> Readers/Users can append multiple response comments.</li>
  <li><strong>Post to Comment (One-to-Many):</strong> A single blog document stores individual referenced comments.</li>
</ul>
</div>
